  "narrative": "I reviewed all 12 new discovery results as a critical audit. Because these are observational associations across 12 pre-specified comparisons, I require both a clear direction, statistical precision compatible with a clinically meaningful difference, and a magnitude near or above a 10% relative difference on the absolute outcome scale. None of the estimates reaches conventional significance. Most direct main effects are very small: H1, H4, H5, H6, H7, and H8 have estimates far below a 10% scale-based difference, and H7/H8 are even in the opposite direction from the negative-dependency hypothesis. I therefore reject and close those directional claims in this dataset. H9 is a null age-interaction with an estimate opposite the claimed direction and an interval not reaching a clearly meaningful positive interaction; I reject and close it. Two direct effects remain worth keeping active as unresolved because they are borderline relative to the clinical threshold: H2 for feature_002 on outcome_006 has a signed estimate of about 0.021, roughly a 12% scale-based effect, but its 95% interval includes zero and also includes the opposite direction. H12 for feature_045 within feature_009 level_003 has a signed estimate of about 0.016, below the 10% central threshold but with an interval reaching plausible clinical magnitude, so I keep it unresolved and active. Three additional comparisons are unresolved but deferred: H3 has a small central effect but a wide interval that cannot exclude a large effect; H10 and H11 are wide interaction estimates, with H11's central estimate near the threshold because outcome_014 has a small absolute mean. I did not request independent validation yet: none of these results is strong enough to justify using validation on a weakly supported discovery claim. Instead, I registered targeted follow-ups: same-predictor main-effect tests for feature_002 across several dependency outcomes, a specificity interaction for feature_045 within feature_009 level_003, and simple-effect/interaction follow-ups for H10/H11. This approach separates exploratory signal from accepted findings and avoids causal or generalization language.",
  "research_notes": "Discovery round 1 appraisal: no accepted claims yet. Closed null directional findings: H1, H4, H5, H6, H7, H8, H9. Active unresolved: H2 (feature_002/outcome_006, borderline), H12 (feature_045 in feature_009 level_003, borderline/uncertain). Deferred unresolved: H3 (wide), H10 (wide interaction), H11 (small mean outcome_014, central near threshold). Next analysis priorities: test whether feature_002 shows related dependency associations across outcomes; test feature_045 specificity by interaction contrast; inspect simple effect for feature_060/outcome_014 in high feature_043 group and simple effect for feature_002/outcome_006 in high feature_018 group. Validation deferred until a signal becomes more robust."
}

