ad should be downgraded. H2 overall, H20 lower feature_018, H26 lower-quartile feature_018, H33 outcome_012, H34 outcome_001 in lower feature_018, H13 outcome_001, H15 outcome_008, and H27 post-hoc reversed interaction are either below threshold, imprecise, inconsistent across outcomes, or not replicated by validation. I keep them scientifically unresolved in status but close them to active follow-up because the evidence does not justify further investment. The feature_045 leads are also closed for now: H12/H22 for outcome_012 and H25/H28/H35/H36/H37 for outcome_014 are either too imprecise or not clinically coherent after localization.\n\nNegative dataset-specific findings include H1, H4-H8, H9, H10, H13, H14, H16, H26, H28, H33, H34, H37, and H40: these comparisons did not support clinically meaningful associations in their registered directions. Unresolved uncertainty remains around H3 and H11 for feature_060/outcome_014, the untested controls H30-H32, and the pending feature_042 refinements H42-H47 plus H48. The most informative next analyses are the feature_042/outcome_014 localizations: stability across feature_018 halves, common feature_009 level_003 context and feature_009 interaction, and cross-outcome checks on outcome_012 and outcome_006. If these remain broadly positive with reasonable precision, the accepted association can be characterized more precisely; if the effect attenuates or is highly stratum/outcome-specific, the accepted claim should be narrowed rather than generalized.",
